    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "**Question:** What is a class and object in OOP?"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Short Answer"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "A class is a blueprint defining properties and methods. An object is an instance of a class with actual data."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Detailed Explanation"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Classes define structure (fields) and behavior (methods). Objects are concrete instances created from classes. Classes support encapsulation, inheritance, and polymorphism."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Example"
